{
  "_comment": [
    "The TDD mandate is ON by default in every repository. This file only lists",
    "the exceptions, so an empty exempt_repos means 'enforced everywhere'.",
    "",
    "The gate blocks two things: a commit whose implementation files were edited",
    "before their test (code_first), and a commit that touches implementation with",
    "no test file in the diff at all (no_tests). Order is read from the session",
    "transcript; when it cannot be known -- no transcript, or files staged in an",
    "earlier session -- the order check is skipped but a test must still be",
    "present, because that is decided from the index alone.",
    "",
    "Exempt automatically: anything the review gate would not call code. The rule",
    "is inverted rather than a second list -- if the path is not in",
    "SOURCE_EXTENSIONS (src/hooks/lib/source-files.js) then no test is required.",
    "That covers docs, data, markup and config (.md, .rst, .txt, .csv, .css,",
    ".html, .json, .yaml, .toml, lockfiles, dotfiles, extensionless files) plus",
    "anything under features/, tmp/ or .planning/. Code needs a test, and shell",
    "scripts are code.",
    "",
    "Two ways to exempt a repository:",
    "  1. touch <repo>/.claude/tdd-mandate.disabled  -- visible in the tree, and",
    "     the same convention as .claude/feature-tracking.disabled;",
    "  2. add its absolute path to exempt_repos below -- for repositories whose",
    "     contents you do not control.",
    "",
    "Paths are matched case-insensitively, ignoring a trailing slash and with",
    "backslashes normalised, so a Windows path may be written either way. A file",
    "that will not parse does NOT disable the mandate: a typo here must not",
    "silently switch off gating everywhere."
  ],
  "exempt_repos": []
}
